# Milestone: v0.14.0-refoundation
# Covers: `every` armed by a deployed script keeps firing after the chunk
#         returns, and `tag.stop()` from inside the body is what ends the
#         run.  The canonical robotics idiom, on the path a deployed
#         script actually takes.
#
#         Before the CLI grew its own pump loop the periodic never fired
#         at all: the chunk armed the timer, `urbi_run` came back because
#         nothing was READY, and the process exited 0 having run none of
#         the body.  It also pins the other half -- the pump stops on its
#         own once the tag is stopped, rather than spinning on an empty
#         timer heap.
#
#         The body is written with `;` separators deliberately: `every (P)
#         A | B` currently parses B INTO the body closure, so a `|` here
#         would test the parser rather than the pump.
# matrix-row: temporal-every

## mode: file
## timeout: 10

var n = 0;
var t = Tag.new();
echo("armed");
t: every(2ms) { n = n + 1; echo(n); if (n >= 3) { t.stop() } }
[00000000] *** armed
[00000000] *** 1
[00000000] *** 2
[00000000] *** 3
